<h1 class="mt-3">Help & Support</h1>
<p class="text-muted" style="font-size:14px;">Answers to common questions</p>

<h2>How do I register?</h2>
<p>Click <a href="/register" style="color:#04888D;">Register</a> and choose your role — Citizen, Organization, or
    Community Admin. Fill in the required details and submit. Citizens receive a verification email; organizations and
    community admins are reviewed by an admin before approval.</p>

<h2>Why is my organization under review?</h2>
<p>Organizations and community admins must be verified before they can post. A system admin reviews your submitted
    verification document. This usually takes 1–2 business days. You will receive an email once your account is approved
    or if more information is needed.</p>

<h2>How do I report a post?</h2>
<p>On any post, click the flag icon in the action row. Select a reason from the list and optionally add a note. Our
    admin team will review the report and take action if the post violates community guidelines.</p>

<h2>How do I volunteer?</h2>
<p>Find a volunteer post in the home feed or explore page. Open the post and click "Join as Volunteer". Fill in your
    name, phone number, and an optional note. The organizer will review your signup and mark attendance after the event.
</p>

<h2>How do alerts work?</h2>
<p>Alerts are location-based posts for urgent local issues. On the Alerts page, you can view all active alerts on a map.
    Use "Use current location" to filter alerts near you. Alerts are posted by verified community admins and
    organizations.</p>

<h2>I forgot my password. What do I do?</h2>
<p>On the login page, click <a href="/forgot-password" style="color:#04888D;">Forgot password?</a>. Enter your
    registered email and we will send a reset link valid for 10 minutes.</p>

<h2>How do I contact support?</h2>
<p>For issues not covered here, email us at <a href="mailto:support@localconnect.np"
        style="color:#04888D;">support@localconnect.np</a>. Include your registered email and a description of the
    issue.</p>